{
  "format": "donna-known-poses/2",
  "provenance": {
    "module": "demo/js/robots/donna/donna-data.js",
    "datasetHash": "71f4bb899e323d98663e303fa485e6835824b6466eb793911caf692806cb1836",
    "formatVersion": "donna-team-v2",
    "derivation": "Every value is read out of the emitted mission module and composed with an FK written from the URDF rig table, never from donna/scene.js. Sample-exactness of the module against the raw MCAPs is the Phase 1 verifier and donna-decode.test.mjs gate, not this one; this fixture freezes what the module says so the SCENE can be held to it.",
    "torsoLocalFrame": "visualInstances[].torsoLocalXYZ are ROS metres in the TORSO LINK frame: bone_local[bucket] * pre_composed * vertex. Field pose, ground lift, heading and the ROS->three frame map are deliberately excluded so a wrong-frame attachment cannot hide behind them.",
    "fixtureCount": "EXACTLY FOUR, and no more are possible: Donna and Rory never fall inside the mission window (window fall counts 0/3/0), so a donna-fallen or rory-fallen fixture would have to be invented. Jack owns every fall.",
    "fallenChoice": "jack-fallen is sampled at t=7.5 s, inside fall 1. The recorded FALLEN enum interval is only 7.137796-7.159246 s (21 ms), which is too narrow to sample robustly, so the fixture binds the prone ATTITUDE at the deepest point of the fall and records the enum honestly (GETTING_UP). The 21 ms FALLEN interval itself is asserted separately by the test."
  },
